### Demo requests. IntelliJ / VS Code (REST Client extension) can run these directly.

### 1. Create an incident
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Checkout payments failing with 500 errors",
  "serviceName": "payment-service",
  "description": "Customers cannot pay since about 10:00. Error rate above 40%.",
  "severity": "CRITICAL"
}

### 2. Run the AI agents on incident 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/1/triage

### 3. Human approves the proposed fix
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/1/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reviewer": "divakar", "comment": "Plan looks right, adding the index first." }

### 4. Mark it resolved
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/1/resolve

### 5. List incidents waiting for approval
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents?status=PENDING_APPROVAL

### Other demo services: order-service (OOMKilled), auth-service (expired TLS certificate)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Order service keeps restarting",
  "serviceName": "order-service",
  "description": "Pods in CrashLoopBackOff every night around 10:00",
  "severity": "HIGH"
}
